      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2014 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Obesity promotes chronic activation of mTORC1 and is a known risk factor for hepatic injury, inflammation, and carcinogenesis. In this issue, Umemura et al. (2014) demonstrate that a persistent reduction in hepatic mTORC1 activity also promotes cell damage and inflammation and sensitizes the liver to cancer development."
